draft_notes.limitations:
No tests were run. The program assumes the constructor's domain:
- exactly two pieces, not 8-adjacent to each other;
- each piece is connected and carries one straight marker run;
- both markers have the same length;
- the grid uses exactly three colours.

If the markers allow no pair of opposite directions, the program falls back to the first candidate direction, matching the archived solver. The supplied fixtures are consistent with the uniform rule; I found no contradictions.
